  "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
  "body": "So, you can work around the problem by defining a [custom image format handler](https://artraweditor.github.io/Customformats). Create a file in `$HOME/.config/ART/imageio/vuescan-tiff.txt` (assuming you are on Linux or macOS) with the following content:\n\n```text\n[ART RAWImageIO]\nExtension=tif\nReadCommand=python3 nonraw.py\n\n[Metadata]\nExif.Image.Software=re:^VueScan.*\n```\n\nThen, create a file `$HOME/.config/ART/imageio/nonraw.py` with the following content:\n\n```python\n# no op file, intentionally does nothing\n```\n\nThen, clear the cache, and now the file should be rendered properly.\n\nLet me know how it works,\nHTH",
